<p><strong>Main Effects:</strong></p>

<DisplayEquation equation="\\text{Effect}_A = \\frac{(1.8 + 2.0) - (2.5 + 3.2)}{2} = -0.95" title="" />


<DisplayEquation equation="\\text{Effect}_B = \\frac{(3.2 + 2.0) - (2.5 + 1.8)}{2} = +0.45" title="" />

<p><strong>Interaction Effect:</strong></p>

<DisplayEquation equation="\\text{Effect}_{AB} = \\frac{(2.5 + 2.0) - (1.8 + 3.2)}{2} = -0.25" title="" />

<p><strong>Conclusion:</strong></p>
<Itemize>

    <Item>Higher spindle speed reduces roughness.</Item>
    <Item>Higher feed rate increases roughness.</Item>
    <Item>Interaction is minor.</Item>
    <Item>Optimal setting: High spindle speed, Low feed rate.</Item>

</Itemize>

